# PROCEDURAL_CAUSATION.hss

Author: Max Rupplin - MEARVK LLC - 2026

## Purpose

Defines an experimental causal/procedural vocabulary for software scanning.

## Ordered method

ROOT -> METHOD -> CAUSE -> ATTENTION -> ATTENUATION -> CLOSURE

## Root medium

The root medium identifies the software object or container from which the
procedure begins. Parent identity is retained where available.

## Cause chain

Cause may be followed by another cause when the observed state depends on a
prior transformation, dependency, acquisition, update, or procedural event.

## Attention

Attention represents an increase in what the procedure deliberately observes.
It is an observability factor, not a human-value judgment.

## Attenuation

Attenuation records conditions that reduce the effective contribution of a
factor, including uncertainty, unavailable content, limits, or incomplete
observation.

## Closure

Closure is the terminal procedural state. It records that the evaluation path
has ended and must not imply that unobserved content was proven safe.

## Civil and institutional actors

The vocabulary may contain abstract roles such as military actor and voting
actor when modeling institutional context. These are categories of procedure,
not judgments about individual people, political parties, candidates, or
military personnel.
